WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.564
I restored Palm's

00:00:01.376 --> 00:00:02.519
last device and

00:00:02.331 --> 00:00:03.427
brought its OS

00:00:03.966 --> 00:00:05.322
A hobbyist restored

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:06.583
Palm's last device

00:00:06.607 --> 00:00:07.515
and ported its

00:00:07.327 --> 00:00:08.529
webOS to other

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.190
platforms

00:00:09.332 --> 00:00:10.274
keeping a piece

00:00:10.098 --> 00:00:11.289
of mobile history

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:11.866
alive

00:00:12.406 --> 00:00:13.514
Palm’s own OS

00:00:13.373 --> 00:00:14.481
made these devices

00:00:14.293 --> 00:00:15.814
useful and responsive

00:00:15.908 --> 00:00:17.335
but by 2004

00:00:17.477 --> 00:00:18.514
both the company

00:00:18.326 --> 00:00:19.516
and its platform

00:00:19.328 --> 00:00:19.823
were in a

00:00:19.635 --> 00:00:20.589
tough place

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:22.053
The Palm brand

00:00:21.865 --> 00:00:23.032
moved to TCL

00:00:23.091 --> 00:00:24.246
and HP moved

00:00:24.058 --> 00:00:24.907
on to selling

00:00:24.718 --> 00:00:26.098
crappy Android and

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:27.218
Windows 8 tablets

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:28.764
Full story on

00:00:28.575 --> 00:00:29.471
the dashboard
